('asc-biology-forensic-ba', 'specialization', 'Biology: Forensic Biology', 'College of Arts and Sciences', 'Biology: Forensic Biology, BA (current advising sheet)', null, null, 'About 32 credit hours in the major. 32 credit hours of core, required, specialization and elective courses (supporting courses don''t count), at least 25 of them in the biological sciences (BIOCHEM, BIOLOGY, EEOB, MICRBIO, MOLGEN), including three lab courses. Electives are 2000-level or above (3000+ for BIOCHEM and BIOLOGY); up to 3 hours of research, individual study, or internship count. Honors versions substitute freely. BA and BS differ only in the supporting (prerequisite) courses. At least 30 credit hours at the 2000 level or above; C- or better in each major course and a 2.00 GPA across the major; no Pass/Non-Pass. At least half the major''s hours must be Ohio State courses (not AP or transfer credit). A second major needs at least 18 hours that don''t overlap with the first. Up to two GE Theme courses (one Citizenship, one other Theme) may count on the major; GE Foundation courses may not.', 'https://clse.osu.edu/students/requirements/forensic-biology', 421, '{}'::text[], 'asc-ba', null, null, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::jsonb),
('asc-biology-forensic-bs', 'specialization', 'Biology: Forensic Biology', 'College of Arts and Sciences', 'Biology: Forensic Biology, BS (current advising sheet)', null, null, 'About 32 credit hours in the major. 32 credit hours of core, required, specialization and elective courses (supporting courses don''t count), at least 25 of them in the biological sciences (BIOCHEM, BIOLOGY, EEOB, MICRBIO, MOLGEN), including three lab courses. Electives are 2000-level or above (3000+ for BIOCHEM and BIOLOGY); up to 3 hours of research, individual study, or internship count. Honors versions substitute freely. BA and BS differ only in the supporting (prerequisite) courses. At least 30 credit hours at the 2000 level or above; C- or better in each major course and a 2.00 GPA across the major; no Pass/Non-Pass. At least half the major''s hours must be Ohio State courses (not AP or transfer credit). A second major needs at least 18 hours that don''t overlap with the first. Up to two GE Theme courses (one Citizenship, one other Theme) may count on the major; GE Foundation courses may not.', 'https://clse.osu.edu/students/requirements/forensic-biology', 422, '{}'::text[], 'asc-bs', null, null, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::jsonb),
