('asc-cis-bs', 'specialization', 'Computer and Information Science', 'College of Arts and Sciences', 'Computer and Information Science, BS (current advising sheet)', null, null, 'About 75 hours of CSE, math, and science courses. Admission: selective; apply to the major after the pre-major courses (CSE 2221, 2231, 2321, MATH 1151-1152). Same computer-science coursework as Engineering''s BS CSE, with Arts and Sciences GE and a world language instead of more math, science and engineering. Curriculum sheet: https://cse.osu.edu/media/document/2025-08-22/bscis_curriculum_sheet_with_sample_schedule_july2025accessibleread-only.docx At least 30 credit hours at the 2000 level or above; C- or better in each major course and a 2.00 GPA across the major; no Pass/Non-Pass. At least half the major''s hours must be Ohio State courses (not AP or transfer credit). A second major needs at least 18 hours that don''t overlap with the first. Up to two GE Theme courses (one Citizenship, one other Theme) may count on the major; GE Foundation courses may not.', 'https://cse.osu.edu/prospective-students/undergrad/majors/bs-cis-program-information', 436, '{}'::text[], 'asc-bs', null, null, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::jsonb),
('asc-cis-ba', 'specialization', 'Computer and Information Science', 'College of Arts and Sciences', 'Computer and Information Science, BA (current advising sheet)', null, null, 'Major core 32 hours plus 27 hours of program electives; 123 hours total. Admission: selective; apply online in the term you finish the admission courses. The most flexible CIS degree: fewer advanced CSE courses, plus an 18-hour related field. Curriculum sheet: https://cse.osu.edu/media/document/2025-08-22/bacis_ge_curriculum_sheet_with_sample_schedule-july2025accessible.docx At least 30 credit hours at the 2000 level or above; C- or better in each major course and a 2.00 GPA across the major; no Pass/Non-Pass. At least half the major''s hours must be Ohio State courses (not AP or transfer credit). A second major needs at least 18 hours that don''t overlap with the first. Up to two GE Theme courses (one Citizenship, one other Theme) may count on the major; GE Foundation courses may not.', 'https://cse.osu.edu/ba-cis-program-information', 437, '{}'::text[], 'asc-ba', null, null, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::jsonb),
('asc-comm-scm-ba', 'specialization', 'Communication: Strategic Communication', 'College of Arts and Sciences', 'Communication: Strategic Communication, BA (current advising sheet)', null, null, 'About 35 credit hours in the major. Admission: competitive Major & Specialization Application after COMM 1100 and 1101. At least 30 credit hours at the 2000 level or above; C- or better in each major course and a 2.00 GPA across the major; no Pass/Non-Pass. At least half the major''s hours must be Ohio State courses (not AP or transfer credit). A second major needs at least 18 hours that don''t overlap with the first. Up to two GE Theme courses (one Citizenship, one other Theme) may count on the major; GE Foundation courses may not.', 'https://comm.osu.edu/undergraduate/communication/scm', 438, '{}'::text[], 'asc-ba', null, null, null, '{}'::text[], '{}'::jsonb),
